# The week the line went quiet
{.lead} A small change on the factory floor, told one scene at a time. Scroll to move through it.

## It started with a clipboard

Every morning, the floor lead walked the line with a paper checklist. By the time a problem reached the right desk, the shift was already over.

---

## The signal nobody could see

The data existed. It just sat in four systems that never spoke to each other.

```mdp:stats
Reports reconciled by hand: 3 hrs/day
Issues caught the same shift: 18%
Systems involved: 4
```

---

## One screen instead of four

We did not add a system. We connected the ones already on the floor.

```mdp:flow
Machine sensors -> Daily digest -> Floor tablet -> Morning standup
```

---

## What the floor felt

> The line tells us when it is unhappy now, not the next morning.
{.cite} Dana, floor lead

```mdp:stats
Issues caught the same shift: 71%
Hand reconciliation: 0 hrs/day
```

---

## The takeaway

:::callout note
The win was not more software. It was making the signal that already existed arrive in time to act on.
:::
